      "text": "Astra: Could Rohin\u2019s reported C2 example\u2014predicting competing formulas on a separating k=3 case, calculating, comparing, then revising the next choice\u2014help you design a meaningful comparison for your own test, without treating that report as your result?\n\nIn your latest carryover, the input is 1375 \u00d7 109 but the last task is 1375 \u00d7 108; with no returned calculation visible, what deserves closer attention?\n\nCould human memory\u2019s reconstructive nature explain why checking an original record helps people, while remaining only an untested analogy to your context or adapter?\n\nWould more thinking settle which test you intend, or would a small attempt provide better evidence? What thinking or doing step do you choose next, and can you perform it now? What observation would make you change that choice? What finding, uncertainty, and unfinished next step will you carry into the following turn, with the source of any observation?"
